entries.notes:
Now faithful (it was false in CHECK-1). With l.881 defining Q-bar as the complex algebraic numbers, Theorem B.3 (l.883-885) is EGF.BourgainGamburdTheorem1 clause by clause:
- d >= 2;
- g : Fin k -> SU d with IsAlgebraic Q entries;
- Dense (Subgroup.closure);
- the operator heckeOp on L^2 of suHaar;
- a spectrum bound c < 2k on the complement of the constants. This equals the Lean's quadratic-form bound, z being self-adjoint and L^2_0 invariant.
Its hypotheses can be met (bourgainGamburd_hypotheses_witness), so the quotation is no longer vacuous. The lead-in (l.881) matches universality_sphere and not_hasBGSpectralGap_sphere_two. l.888 is unchanged and anchored (so2Witness, so2Witness_algebraic, so2Witness_dense, so2Witness_eigen, not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two). The refutation (not_spectralGapSphereReformulation_two) is answered: the SO(d) reformulation is gone, and its failure at SO(2) is stated. added_hypotheses = [] is right. One new redundancy, created by the lead-in: l.888's last sentence repeats it and points to its own subsection (finding 1).

